do_1 = "Use PortableBoundary::decode_with_header with execution.record.header() for the raw leaf at programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/tests/terminal_trap.rs:70 and every raw leaf in tests/market_sandbox_profile.rs:816; preserve both existing test names and all their assertions, including terminal trap reconstruction, integer output, authority refusals and trace commitments."
do_2 = "Add a private decode_captured_boundary helper in programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/examples/market_sandbox_capture.rs taking a raw leaf, the associated ReplayRecordHeader and the existing byte bound, returning the result of PortableBoundary::decode_with_header; route every captured and claimed leaf decode in prepare at lines 286, 302, 304, 325 and 329 through it with execution.record.header(), retaining the raw bytes used by merkle and provider claims. Issue #1914 separately describes the proof-file envelope emission defect at examples/market_sandbox_capture.rs:149."
do_3 = "Add a top-level test capture_record_header_decodes_real_integer_and_trap_leaves in the capture example that uses the genuine runtime producer, as tests/market_sandbox_profile.rs:729 does, to capture integer and trap executions, passes their raw leaves and record header through decode_captured_boundary, asserts the integer result and terminal trap, and checks the raw-leaf Merkle root against execution.record.boundary_root(); run it together with terminal_trap_replay_recomputes_the_claimed_trap_before_committing_the_trace and raw_market_engine_integer_trap_and_sdk_profile_codecs by exact name without requiring an external corpus."
